1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,900
Every chart hides a line — a diagonal.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,600
And when price breaks it… things happen.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,900
More than two thousand stocks
are worth watching.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,800
You can't watch them all. Nobody can.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,600
This is Diago. Every night, it redraws the
trendlines of over two thousand stocks.

6
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,400
And when one closes above its diagonal —

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,000
you get the alert. With a score.

8
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,400
It works the other way too.

9
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:34,900
A stock falls back to its rising
support line… holds, and bounces.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,700
Diago's strongest setup.

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,600
Every signal gets a calibrated
confidence score.

12
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,200
And every signal is tracked publicly —
winners and losers.

13
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,600
Nothing deleted. Ever.

14
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:52,400
Diago. Your ranked shortlist,
ready before the market opens.

15
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:56,000
Seven days free,
then five dollars a month.

16
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:59,800
Statistics — not promises.
Never investment advice.
